  "summary": "Escapes UTF-8 encoded C1 control characters (U+0080 through U+009F) in `BCLog::LogEscapeMessage`. The function detects the two-byte sequences `0xC2 0x80` to `0xC2 0x9F` and formats them as hex escape sequences (`\\x..\\x..`) while leaving other valid UTF-8 sequences untouched.",
  "problem": "`LogEscapeMessage` escapes ASCII controls below 0x20 and 0x7F, but allows two-byte UTF-8 C1 control codes. VTE-based terminal emulators like GNOME Terminal interpret these characters as terminal control sequences (such as CSI, OSC, and DCS), allowing untrusted data printed to logs to drive or corrupt the terminal display.",
  "evidence": [
